      },
      "message": "feat(xtask): gate heavy --covers for one heavy run per merge wave\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --covers <PR>:<head sha>` (repeatable) runs the\nheavy lanes on the trial tree of a merge wave. It refuses a sha that is\nnot a commit, a head that is not an ancestor of HEAD, and a dirty tree.\nIt prints `covers: #<PR> <sha>` and `tree: <HEAD^{tree}>` in the plan\nheader and under the summary, and writes covers.txt to the gate logs.\nThe gate parsing moves to gate_args.rs (main.rs under 400 lines).\n\nAGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gets the wave form beside the PR form.\nThe gate, merge-ready and review-prs skills and PR-reviewer step 5 say\nhow the trial tree is made, how the run is recorded, and when a reviewer\naccepts a wave record. Decision: docs/decisions/3460-heavy-run-per-wave.md.\n\nFixes #3460\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
